Package: apexog
Type: Package
Title: Plausibly Exogenous Bounds for Average Partial Effects in Binary-Outcome IV Models
Version: 0.21.0
Authors@R: person("Jesper N.", "Wulff", email = "jwulff@econ.au.dk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Sensitivity analysis for instrumental-variables models with a
    binary outcome when the exclusion restriction may be violated, following
    Conley, Hansen and Rossi (2012) <doi:10.1162/REST_a_00139>.  The violation
    enters the latent index as an offset; the target is the average partial
    effect (or an average interaction effect) on the probability scale,
    estimated by a control-function probit with Murphy-Topel two-step standard
    errors or by a recursive bivariate probit.  Provides the union of
    confidence intervals over an assumed violation range and the local-to-zero
    interval under a prior on the violation.  R port of the Stata command
    'apexog'.
